Every number in the table is derived by the same three operations:

Probe one basis vector (Section B, C).

Transpose column form to row form for the RTL (Section D).

AND-XOR-reduce the row mask against the input (Section E).

The pipelining (Section G, H) does not change the math — it only partitions the AND-XOR-reduce into narrower stages. The correction (Section I, J) is inversion of the forward map, computed either by Gauss-Jordan or by reverse-stepping; both routes agree on every case ever tested, from the 4-bit toy in this document up to the full 32-bit, 1024-bit design with 129 correction matrices.

